    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "463d7ae6_0046c64e",
        "filename": "chip/g/i2cs.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-14T20:47:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so, the condition will be detected and addressed after 6 seconds, right?\ncan we make this interval shorter?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d908b417075a7e169917cd60dd00b0f245c80dbf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b44e2a0_ecb47961",
        "filename": "chip/g/i2cs.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-14T20:50:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "its up to six seconds, 4.5 seconds on average.\n\nWhat do you think polling interval should be?",
      "parentUuid": "463d7ae6_0046c64e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d908b417075a7e169917cd60dd00b0f245c80dbf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "698b8787_5107e197",
        "filename": "chip/g/i2cs.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-14T23:17:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure if I\u0027m right below, but here\u0027s some reasoning:\n\nEven at 100 kHz (we run at 400), one bit is sent every 10us. If SDA is low, in theory, after 10 bits, or 0.1ms (may be plus some internal processing delays), we should see a byte received/sent. Even with i2cs_read_irq_count incrementing after receiving the entire buffer only, the max size of that buffer is 64 bytes, if I understand the _i2cs_write_complete_int() logic correctly. We don\u0027t do any clock stretching. So, in any case we should be done after \u003c10ms, unless the host resets in the middle of transmission (and this is exactly the case we are trying to address).\n\nBtw (though not directly related), when determining if the bus is busy, the host-side i2c controller driver waits for 20ms.\n\nPolling every ~10ms does seem to be excessive, though.",
      "parentUuid": "8b44e2a0_ecb47961",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d908b417075a7e169917cd60dd00b0f245c80dbf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a328f61_de1d589f",
        "filename": "chip/g/i2cs.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-15T00:52:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we sure don\u0027t have 3 seconds to reliably detect this condition, your calculations make sense.\n\nI just don\u0027t think we have to recover extremely quickly, few seconds seems fine to me, especially given how seldom this condition occurs.\n\nOn top of that I don\u0027t want this to be a burden on the Cr50 CPU, so this is why I picked 3 second interval, seems good enough to me, but I am open for improvement suggestions :)",
      "parentUuid": "698b8787_5107e197",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d908b417075a7e169917cd60dd00b0f245c80dbf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "600523dc_916b7543",
        "filename": "chip/g/i2cs.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-15T01:24:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Absolutely agree re burden. And 10ms is unrealistic. How about 100/200/300ms instead of 3s? Is that too much?\n\nIn general, now, if we wait \u003e ~3*20 ms (3 retries for each command), sending the tpm command, if it happens at this moment, will fail at the driver level. And some upper-level logic may ignore the specifics of the error and decide that the error is unrecoverable. The consequences may vary from transparently retrying later to unexpected login failures or other weird behavior to potentially loss of data (though that should be prevented in those upper layers, if possible now). \n\nIn all cases, it is the responsibility of the callers to retry for some time before giving up in case of comm errors. But the shorter the potential wait, the better. E.g. for cases like TPM_Startup sent by f/w on resume, where we can\u0027t move forward until the command succeeds.",
      "parentUuid": "7a328f61_de1d589f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d908b417075a7e169917cd60dd00b0f245c80dbf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "938de1e2_5e714d73",
        "filename": "chip/g/i2cs.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-15T01:34:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I look at it slightly differently: the failure is extremely rare, one needs to run thousands of cycles of tests to trigger the failure on a subset of devices under test. \n\nWhen the failure happens, the only respite is reboot of the device, which is unacceptable, and this is what this patch is meant to assure to avoid.\n\nI.e., this patch is a fallback for this extremely rare failure case, even if a user experiences some interim issue, it is not a big deal IMO.\n\nIncreasing polling interval reduces consumed power (not sure how significantly). Let\u0027s discuss this offline.",
      "parentUuid": "600523dc_916b7543",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 148,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d908b417075a7e169917cd60dd00b0f245c80dbf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
